  "body": "## What to build\n\nSupport multi-seat indexable milling cutter bodies (face mills and indexable end mills) on the component assembly model.\n\n1. Allow a milling `ToolItem` (cutter body) to declare multiple insert seats (`CSW1_1..CSW1_N`, or a parametric seat count `N` with nominal cutting diameter `DC`, lead angle, max axial depth `APMX`, and `center_cutting` flag) that all reference one shared `CuttingItem` insert.\n2. Extend the assembly resolver in `crates/tools` and `crates/app/src/tool_assembly.rs` to derive milling `Tool` parameters from the body and linked insert:\n   - `diameter`: cutter body nominal cutting diameter `DC`.\n   - `corner_r`: derived from the insert nose radius (or half IC for round button inserts).\n   - `flutes`: `Some(seat_count)`.\n   - `flute_len`: effective axial cutting depth `APMX` (bounded by insert edge length and lead angle).\n   - `center_cutting`: taken from the cutter body (false for face/shell mills, enforcing the M11.3 plunge refusal law).\n   - `tool_material` and `cutting` rows: inherited from the linked insert component.\n3. Combine the cutter body with any spindle arbor, extension, and spindle holder (`BT`, `CAT`, `HSK`, `Weldon`, `ER`) into one judged `HolderProfile` and gauge length.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Depends on the geometry resolver and document commands sub-issues of #2452.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests in `crates/tools` and `crates/app` pin an indexable face mill and an indexable shoulder end mill that both link the same insert component.\n- Tests prove that editing the shared insert updates `corner_r` and cutting data on both mills and marks their milling operations `Stale`.\n- Tests pin spindle collision envelope checks and non-center-cutting plunge refusal on an indexable face mill.\n\nPart of #2452\n",
